IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc8-sch1a`

-- Tests for ssc8-sch1a.l4 (Schedule 1, paragraphs 1 to 3B). Expected values are worked by hand from the paragraph named beside each assertion.

§ `Tests for Schedule 1, paragraphs 1 to 3B`

§§ `Builders (test helpers)`

GIVEN employer IS A STRING
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings`
`sch 1 test a payment` MEANS `sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings` OF employer, amount

-- An election with every fact stated; the three end events are optional.
GIVEN jointly IS A BOOLEAN
      transfer IS A BOOLEAN
      formApproved IS A BOOLEAN
      arrangementsApproved IS A BOOLEAN
      madeDay IS A DATE
      ceased IS A MAYBE DATE
      revoked IS A MAYBE DATE
      terminated IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `sch 1 para 3B an election`
`sch 1 test an election` MEANS `sch 1 para 3B an election` OF jointly, transfer, formApproved, arrangementsApproved, madeDay, ceased, revoked, terminated

`sch 1 test the usual payments` MEANS LIST (`sch 1 test a payment` "A" 100), (`sch 1 test a payment` "A" 50), (`sch 1 test a payment` "B" 70)

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- employed in more than one employment`

-- (1)(a): employer A paid 100 + 50 in the week; employer B paid 70; a stranger paid nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(1)(a) the single payment of earnings in respect of employments under the same employer` FALSE "A" `sch 1 test the usual payments` EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(1)(a) the single payment of earnings in respect of employments under the same employer` FALSE "B" `sch 1 test the usual payments` EQUALS JUST 70
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(1)(a) the single payment of earnings in respect of employments under the same employer` FALSE "C" `sch 1 test the usual payments` EQUALS JUST 0
-- "except as may be provided by regulations": not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(1)(a) the single payment of earnings in respect of employments under the same employer` TRUE "A" `sch 1 test the usual payments` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b): different persons' earnings aggregate in prescribed circumstances: 100 + 50 + 70.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(1)(b) the single payment of earnings paid by different persons in respect of different employments` TRUE `sch 1 test the usual payments` EQUALS JUST 220
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(1)(b) the single payment of earnings paid by different persons in respect of different employments` FALSE `sch 1 test the usual payments` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7): a payment of 100 apportioned 60 and 40 is an apportionment; 60 and 30 is not.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(7) the separate payments of earnings by the employers` 100 (LIST 60, 40) EQUALS JUST (LIST 60, 40)
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(7) the separate payments of earnings by the employers` 100 (LIST 60, 30) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(7) the separate payments of earnings by the employers` 100 (LIST 100) EQUALS JUST (LIST 100)
-- (8): a liability of 90 shared 30 and 60 is; 30 and 50 is not.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(8) the secondary contributors' shares of the liability` 90 (LIST 30, 60) EQUALS JUST (LIST 30, 60)
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(8) the secondary contributors' shares of the liability` 90 (LIST 30, 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(7) and (8) the parts apportioned add up to the whole` 0 EMPTY EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- method of paying Class 1 contributions`

-- (1): the whole of the earner's 80 unless regulations prescribe a part.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE 80 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE 80 (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 30
-- "except in prescribed circumstances": not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE 80 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- earnings not paid to an employed earner, or no liability for both contributions: the sub-paragraph does not speak.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` FALSE TRUE FALSE 80 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` TRUE FALSE FALSE 80 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "to the exclusion of the earner".
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the earner is liable in the first instance for that primary contribution` (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the earner is liable in the first instance for that primary contribution` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the contributions are taken to be paid by the earner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(1) the contributions are taken to be paid by the earner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the entitlement to recover 45 is subject to regulations.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3) the amount the secondary contributor is entitled to recover from the earner` TRUE 45 EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3) the amount the secondary contributor is entitled to recover from the earner` FALSE 45 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): recovery by deduction from earnings and no other way, subject to (3A) to (5).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3) the recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3) the recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3) the recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3B): the employer recovers no more than the regulations allow nor more than it paid: 20 of 35; 35 of 35 where 50 is allowed.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3B) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` TRUE (JUST 20) 35 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3B) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` TRUE (JUST 50) 35 EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3B) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` TRUE NOTHING 35 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(3B) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` FALSE (JUST 20) 35 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): the employee ceased to be employed and received non-monetary earnings after the cessation in the cessation year, or in the next tax year.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(4) sub-paragraph (5) applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(4) sub-paragraph (5) applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(4) sub-paragraph (5) applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(4) sub-paragraph (5) applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): as (3B), where (4) applies.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(5) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 10) 25 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(5) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 40) 25 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(5) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING 25 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(5) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 10) 25 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3(5) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` NOTHING (JUST 10) 25 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3A -- prohibition on recovery of employer's contributions`

-- (1): the three kinds of contribution against the three kinds of act: prohibited.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A secondary Class 1 contributions` `sch 1 para 3A make a deduction from earnings paid by the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A secondary Class 1 contributions` `sch 1 para 3A otherwise recover the contributions from a relevant earner, directly or indirectly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A secondary Class 1 contributions` `sch 1 para 3A enter into an agreement with any person for such a deduction or for such a recovery` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A Class 1A contributions` `sch 1 para 3A make a deduction from earnings paid by the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A Class 1A contributions` `sch 1 para 3A enter into an agreement with any person for such a deduction or for such a recovery` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A Class 1B contributions` `sch 1 para 3A otherwise recover the contributions from a relevant earner, directly or indirectly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A Class 1B contributions` `sch 1 para 3A make a deduction from earnings paid by the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- other contributions, or other acts: the paragraph is silent.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A some other contributions` `sch 1 para 3A make a deduction from earnings paid by the person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `sch 1 para 3A secondary Class 1 contributions` `sch 1 para 3A some other act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): an agreement allowing 500 against 300 payable on relevant employment income: 300 (the smaller). The 2000 Act passed on 28 July 2000 (an input).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 0 (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 200 300 0 (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 200
-- (2A): the part of the agreement within (2A) is disregarded: 300 - 100, and 300 - 400 is nil, not negative.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 100 (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 400 (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 0
-- (3)(a): an agreement entered into before 19th May 2000 authorises nothing; one made on that day does.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 0 (Date 18 5 2000) (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 0 (Date 19 5 2000) (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 300
-- (3)(b): a liability arising before the day of the passing of the 2000 Act: nothing; on that day: allowed.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 0 (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 27 7 2000) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` 500 300 0 (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 28 7 2000) (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS 300
-- (2B): relevant employment income is the three named amounts and no other.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2B) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2B) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of ITEPA 2003` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2B) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) a gain treated as remuneration derived from the earner's employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(2B) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) some other amount` EQUALS FALSE
-- (4): "agreement" includes an arrangement or understanding; anything else is not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(4) the thing is an agreement` `sch 1 para 3A(4) an agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(4) the thing is an agreement` `sch 1 para 3A(4) an arrangement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(4) the thing is an agreement` `sch 1 para 3A(4) an understanding` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(4) the thing is an agreement` `sch 1 para 3A(4) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(4) the earner is a relevant earner` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3A(4) the earner is a relevant earner` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 3B -- transfer of liability to be borne by earner`

-- (1): every element present.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1) this paragraph applies to the election` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- each element missing in turn: the paragraph does not apply.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1) this paragraph applies to the election` (`sch 1 test an election` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1) this paragraph applies to the election` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1) this paragraph applies to the election` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1) this paragraph applies to the election` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A) as 3A(2B).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1A) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1A) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of ITEPA 2003` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1A) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) a gain treated as remuneration derived from the earner's employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(1A) the amount is relevant employment income` `sch 1 para 3A(2B) some other amount` EQUALS FALSE

-- (3): made on 10 January 2005; the first of the three end events is the notice on 1 February (the joint revocation is later, on 1 March).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (JUST (Date 1 2 2005))) (Date 9 1 2005) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (JUST (Date 1 2 2005))) (Date 10 1 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (JUST (Date 1 2 2005))) (Date 31 1 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (JUST (Date 1 2 2005))) (Date 1 2 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (JUST (Date 1 2 2005))) (Date 15 2 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ceased in accordance with its terms on 1 March, nothing else: in force the day before, not on it.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) NOTHING NOTHING) (Date 28 2 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) NOTHING NOTHING) (Date 1 3 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- revoked jointly on 1 March, nothing else.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) NOTHING) (Date 28 2 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) NOTHING) (Date 2 3 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no end event: in force.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` (`sch 1 test an election` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2005) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) (Date 1 1 2040) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` NOTHING (Date 1 1 2040) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (Date 1 3 2005) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` (JUST (Date 1 3 2005)) (Date 28 2 2005) EQUALS FALSE

-- (2): a liability that meets both limbs while the election is in force falls on the earner.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): the scope of an approval.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(4) the approval covers the election` `sch 1 para 3B(4)(a) for an election by the secondary contributor and a particular person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(4) the approval covers the election` `sch 1 para 3B(4)(a) for an election by the secondary contributor and a particular person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(4) the approval covers the election` `sch 1 para 3B(4)(b) for all elections, or elections in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or persons of a particular description` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(4) the approval covers the election` `sch 1 para 3B(4)(b) for all elections, or elections in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or persons of a particular description` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(4) the approval covers the election` `sch 1 para 3B(4)(b) for all elections, or elections in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or persons of a particular description` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): grounds for refusal "shall include" the two named.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(5) the Inland Revenue is entitled to refuse the approval` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(5) the Inland Revenue is entitled to refuse the approval` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(5) the Inland Revenue is entitled to refuse the approval` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(5) the Inland Revenue is entitled to refuse the approval` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): power to withdraw.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(6) the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(6) the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(6) the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(6) the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7A): the withdrawal date is the notice day, or a later day the notice specifies.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7A) the withdrawal date` (Date 1 6 2005) NOTHING EQUALS Date 1 6 2005
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7A) the withdrawal date` (Date 1 6 2005) (JUST (Date 1 9 2005)) EQUALS Date 1 9 2005
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7A) the withdrawal date` (Date 1 6 2005) (JUST (Date 1 5 2005)) EQUALS Date 1 6 2005
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7A) the withdrawal date` (Date 1 6 2005) (JUST (Date 1 6 2005)) EQUALS Date 1 6 2005
-- (7): the election has no effect on the income if (i) or (ii) is met.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7) the election has no effect on the contributions on the income` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7) the election has no effect on the contributions on the income` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7) the election has no effect on the contributions on the income` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7) the election has no effect on the contributions on the income` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7) the election has no effect on the contributions on the income` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7B): void to the extent it relates to (a) and (b): 100 and 50.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7B) the part of the transferred liability for which the election is void` 100 50 EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(7B) the part of the transferred liability for which the election is void` 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- (8): the right to appeal.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): the tribunal's courses.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` TRUE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to refuse an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9)(a) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` TRUE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to withdraw an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9)(a) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` TRUE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to refuse an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9)(b) remit the decision with a direction to make such decision as the tribunal thinks fit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` TRUE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to withdraw an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9)(c) quash the decision and direct that it is to be treated as never having been made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` TRUE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to refuse an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9)(c) quash the decision and direct that it is to be treated as never having been made` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` TRUE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to withdraw an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9) some other course` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` FALSE `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to withdraw an approval` `sch 1 para 3B(9)(a) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (10): income that already counted as employment income under Part 7 of ITEPA 2003.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(10) the election applies to the contributions in respect of the income` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(10) the election applies to the contributions in respect of the income` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(10) the election applies to the contributions in respect of the income` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(10) the election applies to the contributions in respect of the income` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (12)(a): three months on from a day; the period ends the day before, and a short month ends on its last day.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` (Date 28 7 2000) EQUALS Date 28 10 2000
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` (Date 15 11 2000) EQUALS Date 15 2 2001
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` (Date 30 12 2000) EQUALS Date 30 3 2001
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` (Date 31 1 2001) EQUALS Date 1 5 2001
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` (Date 30 11 2000) EQUALS Date 1 3 2001
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` (Date 29 11 2003) EQUALS Date 29 2 2004
-- (12): an election on 27 October 2000, the 2000 Act passed on 28 July 2000 (an input): inside the three months; on 28 October 2000: outside.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` (Date 27 10 2000) (Date 28 7 2000) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` (Date 28 10 2000) (Date 28 7 2000) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` (Date 27 10 2000) (Date 28 7 2000) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an election made before the passing: "before the end of the period" holds on the text's own words.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` (Date 1 6 2000) (Date 28 7 2000) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the reimbursement the secondary contributor is entitled to from the earner` (JUST TRUE) 500 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the reimbursement the secondary contributor is entitled to from the earner` (JUST FALSE) 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(12) the reimbursement the secondary contributor is entitled to from the earner` NOTHING 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (14): the tribunal.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(14) the tribunal is` FALSE EQUALS `sch 1 para 3B(14) the First-tier Tribunal`
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3B(14) the tribunal is` TRUE EQUALS `sch 1 para 3B(14) the Upper Tribunal`

§§ `The regulative twins (traces; check.sh does not see their outcomes: compare both binaries by eye)`

-- 3(1): the secondary contributor pays at time 1: FULFILLED expected.
#TRACE `sch 1 para 3(1) the secondary contributor's duty to pay the earner's primary contribution` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 1 para 3(1) the secondary contributor` DOES `sch 1 para 3(1) pays the earner's primary contribution on the earner's behalf` AT 1

-- 3A(1)(a): the person makes a deduction at time 1: BREACH expected, by the person, with the reason given.
#TRACE `sch 1 para 3A(1) the prohibition on deducting` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions` DOES `sch 1 para 3A(1)(a) makes a deduction from earnings paid by the person` AT 1

-- 3A(1)(a): nothing is done by time 5: the prohibition is respected so far (no event, no breach).
#TRACE `sch 1 para 3A(1) the prohibition on deducting` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

#TRACE `sch 1 para 3A(1) the prohibition on otherwise recovering` AT 0 WITH
